      <h2>Shipping Gold Wash Plants Worldwide</h2>
      <p>We've shipped wash plants to over 40 countries, from Peru's remote mining regions to Papua New Guinea's island operations. After hundreds of international shipments, we've learned what works — and what doesn't. Here's your complete guide to getting your wash plant delivered safely and cost-effectively anywhere in the world.</p>
      
      <h3>Container Sizing: The Foundation of Your Shipping Plan</h3>
      <p>Understanding how wash plants fit in shipping containers is crucial for cost planning:</p>
      
      <ul>
        <li><strong><a href="../products/50-ton">M50 wash plant:</a></strong> Fits perfectly in one 20' container</li>
        <li><strong>Two M50s:</strong> Can ship together in one 20' container (space-efficient)</li>
        <li><strong><a href="../products/100-ton">M100 wash plant:</a></strong> Requires one 40' container</li>
        <li><strong><a href="../products/200-ton">M200 wash plant:</a></strong> Ships in four 40' containers</li>
        <li><strong><a href="../products/300-ton">M300 wash plant:</a></strong> Ships in six 40' containers</li>
      </ul>

