      <h3>CIF vs FOB: Understanding Your Shipping Terms</h3>
      <p>Most of our international customers choose between two shipping arrangements:</p>
      
      <p><strong>FOB (Free on Board) - Port of Los Angeles/Long Beach:</strong></p>
      <ul>
        <li>We deliver to the port and load onto your shipping vessel</li>
        <li>You arrange and pay for ocean freight and destination handling</li>
        <li>You handle customs clearance at destination port</li>
        <li>Best if you have established freight forwarders</li>
        <li>Typically saves 15-25% on total landed cost</li>
      </ul>
      
      <p><strong>CIF (Cost, Insurance, Freight) - Your Destination Port:</strong></p>
      <ul>
        <li>We arrange complete door-to-port delivery</li>
        <li>Includes ocean freight, marine insurance, and export documentation</li>
        <li>You still handle customs clearance and import duties</li>
        <li>Simplest option for first-time international buyers</li>
        <li>We can quote CIF to most major ports worldwide</li>
      </ul>
      
      <h3>Freight Logistics: Real-World Experience</h3>
      <p>Based on our shipments to major mining regions:</p>
      
      <p><strong>To Peru (Callao Port):</strong></p>
      <ul>
        <li>Transit time: 12-16 days from Los Angeles</li>
        <li>Best option: CIF Callao for hassle-free delivery</li>
        <li>Local agent handles customs clearance efficiently</li>
        <li>Road transport to interior mining sites is excellent</li>
      </ul>
      
      <p><strong>To West Africa (Lagos, Tema, Abidjan):</strong></p>
      <ul>
        <li>Transit time: 18-25 days from Los Angeles</li>
        <li>Port infrastructure varies significantly by location</li>
        <li>Customs processing can take 7-14 additional days</li>
        <li>Consider port storage fees in your timeline</li>
      </ul>
      
      <p><strong>To Papua New Guinea (Port Moresby, Lae):</strong></p>
      <ul>
        <li>Transit time: 14-18 days from Los Angeles</li>
        <li>Limited shipping frequency (weekly services)</li>
        <li>Excellent mining equipment handling experience</li>
        <li>Air cargo available for urgent spare parts</li>
      </ul>
      
      <h3>Telex Release and Documentation</h3>
      <p>For smooth customs clearance, ensure these documents are ready:</p>
      
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Commercial Invoice:</strong> Detailed equipment description and values</li>
        <li><strong>Packing List:</strong> Complete parts inventory for each container</li>
        <li><strong>Bill of Lading:</strong> Original or telex release (faster)</li>
        <li><strong>Certificate of Origin:</strong> Required for duty calculations</li>
        <li><strong>Technical Specifications:</strong> May be required by some countries</li>
      </ul>
      
      <p><strong>Telex Release Advantage:</strong> Instead of waiting for original documents to arrive by courier, telex release allows immediate customs processing with electronic documents. This saves 3-5 days and reduces demurrage charges.</p>
      
      <h3>Customs Brokers: Your Essential Partner</h3>
      <p>A good customs broker makes the difference between smooth delivery and weeks of delays. Choose brokers who:</p>
      
      <ul>
        <li>Have specific experience with mining equipment</li>
        <li>Understand HS codes for wash plants (usually 8474.10 or 8474.90)</li>
        <li>Can handle temporary import permits if you're testing equipment</li>
        <li>Offer port storage if customs clearance takes time</li>
        <li>Provide accurate duty and fee calculations upfront</li>
      </ul>
      
      <h3>Timeline Planning: What to Expect</h3>
      <p>Here's the realistic timeline for international wash plant delivery:</p>
      
      <ol>
        <li><strong>Manufacturing:</strong> 4-8 weeks depending on model and options</li>
        <li><strong>Pre-shipment preparation:</strong> 1 week for documentation and container loading</li>
        <li><strong>Ocean transit:</strong> 2-4 weeks depending on destination</li>
        <li><strong>Customs clearance:</strong> 3-10 days (varies greatly by country)</li>
        <li><strong>Inland transport:</strong> 1-5 days depending on distance from port</li>
      </ol>
      
      <p><strong>Total timeline:</strong> Plan for 8-15 weeks from order to delivery at your site.</p>
      
      <h3>Cost Factors and Hidden Expenses</h3>
      <p>Beyond the equipment cost, budget for these shipping-related expenses:</p>
      
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Ocean freight:</strong> $3,000-$15,000 depending on destination and size</li>
        <li><strong>Import duties:</strong> 0-25% of equipment value (varies by country)</li>
        <li><strong>Port handling:</strong> $500-$2,000 per container</li>
        <li><strong>Customs broker fees:</strong> $800-$1,500 for complete clearance</li>
        <li><strong>Inland transport:</strong> $1,000-$5,000+ depending on distance</li>
        <li><strong>Storage fees:</strong> $50-$150 per day if clearance is delayed</li>
      </ul>
      
      <h3>Regional Considerations</h3>
      <p><strong>Africa:</strong> Plan extra time for customs. Port infrastructure varies widely. Consider regional hubs like Durban for southern Africa distribution.</p>
      
      <p><strong>South America:</strong> Peru and Chile have excellent mining equipment import processes. Venezuela and Bolivia have more complex procedures.</p>
      
      <p><strong>Pacific Islands:</strong> Limited shipping schedules require precise timing. Consider air freight for critical spare parts.</p>
      
      <p><strong>Europe:</strong> Excellent logistics but high costs. Consider used equipment options for cost savings.</p>
      
      <h3>Our Shipping Support</h3>
      <p>We don't just manufacture equipment — we're your partner throughout the entire shipping process. Our international shipping team:</p>
      
      <ul>
        <li>Provides detailed shipping cost estimates before you order</li>
        <li>Handles all export documentation and compliance</li>
        <li>Coordinates with your customs broker</li>
        <li>Tracks shipments and provides regular updates</li>
        <li>Provides technical support for customs questions</li>
      </ul>
      
      <p><strong>Ready to ship internationally?</strong> Call Chase at <a href="tel:+18888682650">(888) 868-2650</a> for a complete shipping quote to your location. We'll walk you through every step and connect you with reliable logistics partners in your region.</p>
